    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16001" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĕpĭtăphĭum</span></b> ,
			ii, n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιτάφιον</span>, or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">epitaphius</span></b> , m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιτάφιος
			λόγος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a funeral oration</i>, <i>eulogy.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen., Inscr. 
			 Drell. 1022; 4518.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Esp., of the famous oration of
			Pericles over the fallen Athenians, in Plato's Menexenus, <i><span class="en">Cic. Tusc.
				5, 12, 36</span></i>.</div>
